  "question": {
    "text": "Calculate the volume of water(in mL) required to dissolve 0.1 g lead (II) chloride to get a saturated solution (K<sub>sp</sub> of PbCl<sub>2</sub> = 3.21 × 10<sup>-8</sup>, atomic mass of Pb = 207 u).Report your answer by rounding it up to nearest whole number.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "180",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Suppose solubility of PbCl<sub>2</sub> in water is s mol L<sup>-1</sup>.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtable> <mtr> <mtd> <msub> <mtext>PbCl</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>s</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>⇌</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <msup> <mtext>Pb</mtext> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mo>+</mo> </mrow> </msup> <mtext>(aq)</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <msup> <mtext>2Cl</mtext> <mo>-</mo> </msup> <mtext>(aq)</mtext> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>s</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mtd> <mtd> </mtd> <mtd> <mtext>s</mtext> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>2s</mtext> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable> </mrow> </math><br /><br />K<sub>sp</sub> = [Pb<sup>2</sup><sup>+</sup>] <strong>·</strong> [Cl<sup>-</sup>]<sup>2</sup><br /><br />K<sub>sp</sub> = [s] [2s]<sup>2</sup> = 4s<sup>3</sup><br /><br />3.2 × 10<sup>-8</sup> = 4s<sup>3</sup><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>s</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>3.2</mtext> <mo>×</mo> <msup> <mtext>10</mtext> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>0.8</mtext> <mo>×</mo> <msup> <mtext>10</mtext> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />s<sup>3</sup> = 8.0 × 10<sup>-9</sup><br /><br />Solubility of PbCl<sub>2</sub>, = s = 2 × 10<sup>-3</sup> mol L<sup>-1</sup><br /><br />Solubility of PbCl<sub>2</sub> in gL<sup>-1</sup> = 278 × 2 × 10<sup>-3</sup> = 0.556 g L<sup>-1</sup><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(∵ Molar mass of PbCl<sub>2</sub> = 207 + (2 × 35.5) = 278)<br /><br />0.556 g of PbCl<sub>2</sub> dissolve in 1 L of water.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴</mo> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <msub> <mtext>0.1 g of PbCl</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>will dissolve in</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>×</mo> <mtext>0.1</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>0.556</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>L of water</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />​= 0.1798 L = 179.8 mL",
